OPAL

Performance-first Linux remote desktop.

install

Fedora 44+ / Fedora Asahi
  sudo dnf install -y https://mirrors.rpmfusion.org/free/fedora/rpmfusion-free-release-$(rpm -E %fedora).noarch.rpm
  sudo dnf install -y --allowerasing gcc-c++ make pkgconf-pkg-config SDL3-devel openssl-devel ffmpeg ffmpeg-devel pipewire pipewire-devel pipewire-pulseaudio libportal libportal-devel xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

  GNOME instead of KDE    --> sudo dnf install -y xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
  wlroots instead of KDE  --> sudo dnf install -y xdg-desktop-portal-wlr

CachyOS / Arch Linux
  sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel pkgconf sdl3 openssl ffmpeg pipewire pipewire-pulse libportal xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

  GNOME instead of KDE    --> sudo pacman -S --needed xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
  wlroots instead of KDE  --> sudo pacman -S --needed xdg-desktop-portal-wlr

Debian 13+ / Ubuntu with SDL3
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential pkg-config libsdl3-dev libssl-dev ffmpeg libavformat-dev libavcodec-dev libavutil-dev libswresample-dev libswscale-dev libpipewire-0.3-dev libportal-dev pipewire pipewire-pulse xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

  GNOME instead of KDE    --> sudo apt-get install -y xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
  wlroots instead of KDE  --> sudo apt-get install -y xdg-desktop-portal-wlr

build
  make -j"$(nproc)"
  sudo make install

run
  host/client setup --> opal
  connect           --> opal <connection-code>
  debug             --> OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal <connection-code>
  doctor            --> opal doctor
  test              --> make test
  latency gate       --> make test-hpi

required build/runtime stack
  C++20 compiler + make + pkg-config
  SDL3 --> window, rendering, client input, client clipboard, audio output
  OpenSSL
  FFmpeg executable + libavformat/libavcodec/libavutil/libswresample/libswscale
  PipeWire + PipeWire PulseAudio compatibility service
  libportal
  xdg-desktop-portal + one compositor portal backend
  wl-clipboard on Wayland for host clipboard synchronization
  systemd + udev on the standard install path

Wayland host
  native screen capture --> PipeWire + libportal + xdg-desktop-portal
  clipboard             --> wl-copy + wl-paste from wl-clipboard
  input                 --> /dev/uinput; sudo make install installs the OPAL udev rule and loads uinput when possible
  audio capture         --> PipeWire/PulseAudio compatible default source

client
  window/render/input/clipboard/audio --> SDL3
  video presentation                   --> SDL renderer only

video
  H.264 encode/decode is required.
  OPAL selects available hardware codec paths automatically: VAAPI, V4L2 M2M, NVENC or QSV.
  SDL3 is always the client presentation backend.
  Hardware-decoded frames are normalized to an SDL-supported YUV/NV12 frame before presentation.
  Software codec fallback uses libx264/OpenH264 when available.
  Fedora command above uses RPM Fusion FFmpeg so the full H.264 software fallback is available.
  gpu-screen-recorder is optional only; it is an external capture fallback when native PipeWire capture cannot run.

network
  OPAL uses signed rendezvous + direct encrypted UDP with encrypted relay fallback.
  Tailscale is used when available for the direct tailnet path and can be installed/configured by OPAL when needed; curl is required for automatic installation.
  sudo make install configures OPAL UDP firewall rules when firewalld or UFW is installed.

verify
  opal doctor
  make test-hpi

  host   --> OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal
  client --> OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal <connection-code>

server
  make deploy-rendezvous
